IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Act 1966 (Singapore) -- from law graduate to practising solicitor: who is an "eligible person" (s 2(1)),
-- admission as a lawyer (NP) (ss 11A, 11B), admission as an advocate and solicitor (ss 12, 13, 16), the provisional
-- practising certificate during and after practice training (ss 18, 32(1A)), and the annual practising certificate
-- (ss 25, 26, 32(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 17 April 2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/LPA1966.txt. Parts 2AA, 2A and 2B as substituted or amended by Act 37 of 2023 wef
-- 17 July 2024.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0283 (Haziq scenario, event h031): a law graduate who has completed the Bar course
-- and a six-month practice training contract -- what must happen before he may practise, and what must he renew each year
-- to keep practising?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: what makes a "qualified person" (s 2(1), (2), (3): the Qualified Persons rules); the courses, examinations,
-- practice training period, periods of validity and admission procedure themselves (s 10(2): the Institute's rules -- the
-- Act does not say the training period is six months); the Minister's approvals, deemings, exemptions and abridgments
-- (ss 11C, 14) beyond a flag for each; ad hoc admission of King's Counsel (s 15); striking off for false documents
-- (ss 11D(4), 16(4)); the refusal, conditions and appeal machinery for certificates (ss 19 to 24C, 25A to 25C, 27A to 28);
-- locum solicitors (ss 25(2A), 26(1A)); the Attorney-General's certificates for public-sector and academic solicitors
-- (s 26(2) to (8)); Senior Counsel; foreign lawyers; fees (s 189).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Act 1966 -- admission and practising certificates`

§§ `2(1) -- qualified person, eligible person`

-- s 2(1): "'eligible person' means -- (a) a lawyer (NP); or (b) a person who is approved by the Minister as an eligible
-- person under section 14(1)". "'practice trainee' means a qualified person or eligible person who is serving his or her
-- practice training period". "'practice training period' means the period during which a qualified person or eligible
-- person is required to receive supervised training in relation to the practice of Singapore law before he or she can be
-- admitted as an advocate and solicitor".
--
-- Since 17 July 2024 a law graduate is admitted TWICE: first as a lawyer (NP) (Part 2AA), which makes him an eligible
-- person, and then as an advocate and solicitor (Part 2A).
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `of good character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a qualified person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `law degree conferred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualified only by passing the final law examination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed the lawyer (NP) courses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passed the lawyer (NP) examinations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted from the lawyer (NP) courses and examinations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the roll of lawyers (NP)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Minister as an eligible person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of practice training served` IS A NUMBER
    `practice training period applicable in months` IS A NUMBER
    `exempted from or abridged practice training` IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed the advocate and solicitor courses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passed the advocate and solicitor examinations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted from the advocate and solicitor courses and examinations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class with a prescribed application time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applied within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is an eligible person` IF
        `the candidate`'s `on the roll of lawyers (NP)`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `approved by the Minister as an eligible person`

§§ `11A, 11B -- admission as a lawyer (NP)`

-- s 11A(1): "the court may, in its discretion, and with or without an oral hearing, admit a qualified person as a
-- lawyer (NP) of the Supreme Court". (2)(b), (3): a qualified person in a prescribed class must apply within the prescribed
-- time, and "The court must not admit ... any qualified person who is required, but fails, to comply with subsection
-- (2)(b)". (4): the Attorney-General, the Society and the Institute may object.
-- s 11B(1): "a qualified person must not be admitted as a lawyer (NP) unless he or she -- (a) has attained 21 years of age;
-- (b) is of good character; (c) has attended and satisfactorily completed such courses of instruction as the Board of
-- Directors of the Institute may prescribe under section 10; and (d) has passed such examinations as the Board ... may
-- prescribe". (3): a person qualified "by reason of his or her having passed the final examination for a law degree ...
-- must not be admitted as a lawyer (NP) before the law degree is conferred upon him or her".
-- s 11C(5): the Minister may exempt a qualified person from s 11B(1)(c) and (d) (only -- not from age or character).
--
-- These are conditions without which the court MUST NOT admit. Meeting them does not entitle anyone to admission: the
-- court "may, in its discretion" admit.
GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is in time for admission` IF
        NOT `the candidate`'s `in a class with a prescribed application time`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `applied within the prescribed time`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` IF
        `the candidate`'s `a qualified person`
    AND `the candidate`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the candidate`'s `of good character`
    AND (    (`the candidate`'s `completed the lawyer (NP) courses` AND `the candidate`'s `passed the lawyer (NP) examinations`)
         OR  `the candidate`'s `exempted from the lawyer (NP) courses and examinations`)
    AND (    (NOT `the candidate`'s `qualified only by passing the final law examination`)
         OR  `the candidate`'s `law degree conferred`)
    AND `the application is in time for admission` `the candidate`

§§ `12, 13 -- admission as an advocate and solicitor`

-- s 12(1): "the court may, in its discretion and with or without an oral hearing, admit an eligible person as an advocate
-- and solicitor of the Supreme Court". (2)(a): the application must comply with the rules under s 10(2)(g); (2)(b), (3): an
-- eligible person in a prescribed class must apply within the prescribed time, else "The court must not admit" him. (4): the
-- Attorney-General, the Society and the Institute are entitled to object. (5A): the court may adjourn, allow withdrawal, or
-- make another order, having regard to "the conduct and character of the eligible person".
-- s 13: "an eligible person must not be admitted as an advocate and solicitor unless he or she -- (a) has attained 21 years
-- of age; (b) is of good character; (c) has satisfactorily served the practice training period applicable to him or her;
-- (d) has attended and satisfactorily completed such courses of instruction as the Board of Directors of the Institute may
-- prescribe under section 10; and (e) has passed such examinations as the Board ... may prescribe under section 10".
-- s 14(4), (5): the Minister may exempt from s 13(c), (d) and (e), or abridge the practice training period.
-- s 10(2)(b): the Institute's rules "prescribe the duration of the practice training period applicable to a practice
-- trainee (including different durations for different classes of practice trainees)". The Act fixes no number of months;
-- the applicable period is an INPUT here.
GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate has served the practice training period` IF
        `the candidate`'s `months of practice training served` AT LEAST `the candidate`'s `practice training period applicable in months`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `exempted from or abridged practice training`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` IF
        `the candidate is an eligible person` `the candidate`
    AND `the candidate`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the candidate`'s `of good character`
    AND `the candidate has served the practice training period` `the candidate`
    AND (    (`the candidate`'s `completed the advocate and solicitor courses` AND `the candidate`'s `passed the advocate and solicitor examinations`)
         OR  `the candidate`'s `exempted from the advocate and solicitor courses and examinations`)
    AND `the application is in time for admission` `the candidate`

§§ `16 -- the roll`

-- s 16(2): "The name, with the date of admission, of every person admitted must be entered upon the roll in order of
-- admission." (3): "Every person admitted as an advocate and solicitor must pay the fee prescribed under section 189 ...
-- and the Registrar must deliver to him or her an instrument of admission". Admission puts the name on the roll; it does
-- not by itself let him practise (s 32(1)(b) below).

§§ `18, 32(1A) -- the provisional practising certificate`

-- s 18(1): the section applies to a lawyer (NP) who "(a) is serving his or her practice training period with a Singapore
-- law practice; (b) has served not less than the prescribed period of his or her practice training period in a Singapore
-- law practice ...; and (c) wishes to do any act in the capacity of an advocate and solicitor under the supervision of a
-- solicitor -- (i) during his or her practice training period; and (ii) after the end of that practice training period and
-- before he or she is admitted as an advocate and solicitor". (2): he "must, before doing any act ..., apply to the
-- Registrar for a provisional practising certificate". (6): it "is in force for a period of 12 months starting on the date
-- of the issue or until the lawyer (NP) is admitted as an advocate and solicitor under section 12, whichever is earlier".
-- (5): it does not authorise practice as a locum.
-- s 32(1A): a person may, during those periods, "practise provisionally if -- (a) the person's name is on the roll of
-- lawyers (NP); and (b) the person has in force a provisional practising certificate".
GIVEN `on the roll of lawyers (NP)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `serving training with a Singapore law practice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months served in a Singapore law practice` IS A NUMBER,
      `prescribed months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 18 lets the trainee apply for a provisional practising certificate` IF
        `on the roll of lawyers (NP)`
    AND `serving training with a Singapore law practice`
    AND `months served in a Singapore law practice` AT LEAST `prescribed months`

-- Days are counted from the day of issue (day 0). The certificate covers days 0 to 364 of a 365-day year counted this way,
-- unless he is admitted first. [Inference: "12 months starting on the date of the issue" read as 365 days; a leap year is
-- not modelled.]
GIVEN `days since issue` IS A NUMBER,
      `admitted as an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisional practising certificate is in force` IF
        `days since issue` AT LEAST 0
    AND `days since issue` LESS THAN 365
    AND NOT `admitted as an advocate and solicitor`

§§ `25, 26 -- the practising certificate, every year`

-- s 25(1): "Every solicitor must, IN EVERY YEAR BEFORE he or she does any act in the capacity of an advocate and solicitor,
-- deliver ... to the Registrar an application for a practising certificate", accompanied by declarations of (a) his name,
-- his law practice, and that he is not disqualified under s 26(1); (b) that Society subscriptions, levies and Compensation
-- Fund contributions are paid or arranged, professional indemnity rules complied with, Council penalties and court-ordered
-- sums paid, and rules under s 59(1)(aa) complied with; (c) that Singapore Academy of Law moneys are paid or arranged;
-- (ca) a declaration prescribed by the Institute under s 10; (d) an accountant's report under s 73 or the Council's
-- certificate that none is needed; (da) any other prescribed document; and (e) "the prescribed fee".
-- s 25(2): "The Registrar must, subject to sections 25A, 25AA and 25B, thereupon issue to the solicitor a practising
-- certificate".
DECLARE Application HAS
    `declaration of particulars and no disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declaration of Society payments and indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declaration of Academy payments` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declaration prescribed by the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accountant's report or Council certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other prescribed documents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed fee paid` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is complete under section 25(1)` IF
        `the application`'s `declaration of particulars and no disqualification`
    AND `the application`'s `declaration of Society payments and indemnity`
    AND `the application`'s `declaration of Academy payments`
    AND `the application`'s `declaration prescribed by the Institute`
    AND `the application`'s `accountant's report or Council certificate`
    AND `the application`'s `other prescribed documents`
    AND `the application`'s `prescribed fee paid`

-- s 26(1): "A solicitor must not apply for a practising certificate -- (a) unless -- (i) he or she is practising or intends
-- to practise in a Singapore law practice; (ii) [is registered under s 36E and practises Singapore law in a Joint Law
-- Venture, Qualifying Foreign Law Practice or licensed foreign law practice]; or (iii) ... intends to practise as a locum
-- solicitor; ... (d) if he or she has, for a period of 3 years or more, held office as a Supreme Court Judge [or a Malaysian
-- equivalent]; (e) if he or she is an undischarged bankrupt; (f) if he or she has entered into a composition with his or
-- her creditors or a deed of arrangement ...; (g) if he or she has one or more outstanding judgments against him or her
-- amounting in the aggregate to $100,000 or more which he or she has been unable to satisfy within 6 months from the date
-- of the earliest judgment; or (h) if he or she lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008".
-- (3): s 26(1) does not apply to public-sector and academic solicitors holding an Attorney-General's certificate (not
-- encoded).
DECLARE Solicitor HAS
    `practising or intending to practise in a Singapore law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `practising Singapore law in a foreign or joint practice under section 36E` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intending to practise as a locum` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a former Supreme Court Judge of 3 years or more` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a composition or deed of arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsatisfied judgments in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the earliest unsatisfied judgment` IS A NUMBER
    `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the solicitor` IS A Solicitor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solicitor is caught by section 26(1)(g)` IF
        `the solicitor`'s `unsatisfied judgments in dollars` AT LEAST 100000
    AND `the solicitor`'s `months since the earliest unsatisfied judgment` AT LEAST 6

GIVEN `the solicitor` IS A Solicitor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` IF
        (    `the solicitor`'s `practising or intending to practise in a Singapore law practice`
         OR  `the solicitor`'s `practising Singapore law in a foreign or joint practice under section 36E`
         OR  `the solicitor`'s `intending to practise as a locum`)
    AND (NOT `the solicitor`'s `a former Supreme Court Judge of 3 years or more`)
    AND (NOT `the solicitor`'s `an undischarged bankrupt`)
    AND (NOT `the solicitor`'s `in a composition or deed of arrangement with creditors`)
    AND (NOT `the solicitor is caught by section 26(1)(g)` `the solicitor`)
    AND (NOT `the solicitor`'s `lacks capacity`)

-- s 25(2) read with ss 25A, 25AA: the Registrar must issue unless the Attorney-General or the Council has asked him to
-- refuse (s 25A(2)(a)) or he refuses for non-payment (s 25AA). The refusal is an INPUT here.
GIVEN `the solicitor` IS A Solicitor,
      `the application` IS AN Application,
      `refused under section 25A or 25AA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must issue the practising certificate` IF
        `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `the solicitor`
    AND `the application is complete under section 25(1)` `the application`
    AND NOT `refused under section 25A or 25AA`

-- s 25(3): "Every practising certificate ... subject to sections 26(9) and 27B, is in force from the date of issue to the end
-- of the year." (6): "'year' means the period from 1 April in any calendar year to 31 March in the next calendar year."
-- (5): "Every practising certificate issued in the month of April is deemed to have been in force from the first day of
-- that month."
-- So every certificate dies on 31 March, however late in the year it was issued, and a new one is needed for each
-- April-to-March year.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the practice year begins in` `month` `calendar year` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

-- The calendar year whose 31 March ends the certificate.
GIVEN `issue month` IS A NUMBER, `issue year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the practising certificate expires on 31 March of` `issue month` `issue year` MEANS
    `the practice year begins in` `issue month` `issue year` + 1

-- A date as one number, yyyymmdd.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`date key` d m y MEANS y * 10000 + m * 100 + d

-- The day from which the certificate counts as in force: the date of issue, or 1 April if issued in April.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`in force from` d m y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 4 THEN `date key` 1 4 y ELSE `date key` d m y

GIVEN `issue day` IS A NUMBER, `issue month` IS A NUMBER, `issue year` IS A NUMBER,
      `day` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practising certificate is in force on` IF
        `date key` `day` `month` `year` AT LEAST `in force from` `issue day` `issue month` `issue year`
    AND `date key` `day` `month` `year` AT MOST `date key` 31 3 (`the practising certificate expires on 31 March of` `issue month` `issue year`)

-- s 26(9): a practising certificate "ceases to be in force -- (a) when the solicitor ceases to practise or to be employed as
-- provided in this section; (b) upon the solicitor becoming subject to any disqualification under subsection (1)(e), (f),
-- (g) or (h); or (c) when the Registrar subsequently issues another practising certificate". s 25(4): it expires
-- immediately if his name is removed from or struck off the roll. (Not modelled as dates; see the s 32 rule below.)

§§ `32(1) -- no practice without both`

-- s 32(1): "a person must not practise as an advocate and solicitor or do any act as an advocate and solicitor unless --
-- (a) his or her name is on the roll of advocates and solicitors; and (b) he or she has in force a practising certificate."
GIVEN `on the roll of advocates and solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `practising certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 32(1) allows him to act as an advocate and solicitor` IF
        `on the roll of advocates and solicitors`
    AND `practising certificate in force`
